// Teksty wlasne (nie z gry).
@101 = ~mul~
@102 = ~Mul~
@103 = ~MUL: Muls are the sterile offspring of humans and dwarves, bred in the slave pits of Athas for labor and the arena. They combine human height with dwarven bulk and are famed for their endurance.

Advantages:
+4 Strength
+2 Constitution

Disadvantages:
-2 Charisma

(Dark Sun 3.5e. Level adjustment +1: -35% experience.)~
@104 = ~half-giant~
@105 = ~Half-Giant~
@106 = ~HALF-GIANT: Huge descendants of giants and humans, bred by the sorcerer-kings as soldiers and slaves. Half-giants have tremendous strength and dull wits, and imitate the ways of those they admire.

Dark Sun 3.5e: +8 Strength, -2 Dexterity, +4 Constitution, -4 Intelligence, -4 Wisdom, -4 Charisma. Large size: +2 natural armor and -1 AC from size (net +1 AC), -1 to hit. Darkvision. Faster movement. Level adjustment +2 (-50% experience).

In the game a half-giant looks like a half-orc and has no reach.~

// --- Podklasy (komponent 2). Nazwy i opisy robocze - do decyzji wlasciciela. ---
@201 = ~templar~
@202 = ~Templar~
@203 = ~TEMPLAR: Priest-bureaucrats of the sorcerer-kings: judges, tax collectors and secret police of the city-states. A templar draws divine spells from the sorcerer-king through his sigil and casts them spontaneously, like a sorcerer.

Sorcerer subclass (Dark Sun 3.5e). Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Will. Skill points: 4 per level. Class skills: Bluff, Concentration, Diplomacy, Intimidate, Knowledge, Spellcraft.

Spells: templar spell list (divine, cast with Charisma). Not possible: turning undead, domain spells and the secular authority powers of the Dark Sun rules.~
@204 = ~Templar: Secular Aptitude and Assume Domain (powers of the sorcerer-king's city) - description only.~
@211 = ~Barbarian~
@212 = ~athasian barbarian~
@213 = ~Athasian Barbarian~
@214 = ~ATHASIAN BARBARIAN: Born in the wastes beyond the city-states, these warriors survive the burning sun and the silt storms of Athas through sheer endurance.

(Experimental barbarian subclass: Dark Sun conversion test. No special abilities yet.)~
@221 = ~earth cleric~
@222 = ~Earth Cleric~
@223 = ~EARTH CLERIC: On Athas the gods are silent, and clerics draw their power from the elemental planes. Clerics of Earth revere stone and soil, the foundations that endure even under the dying sun.

(Experimental cleric patron: Dark Sun conversion test. No domain bonuses yet.)~

// --- Polelf atasyjski (komponent 3). Nazwy i opisy robocze - do decyzji wlasciciela. ---
@111 = ~athasian half-elf~
@112 = ~Athasian Half-Elf~
@113 = ~ATHASIAN HALF-ELF: On Athas half-elves belong to neither of their parents' peoples. Shunned by humans and elves alike, most learn to live alone in the wastes and rely on no one but themselves.

Advantages:
+2 Dexterity
+2 Constitution

Disadvantages:
-2 Intelligence
-2 Charisma

(Experimental subrace: Dark Sun conversion test.)~

// --- Nowe podklasy (komponent 2). Nazwy i opisy robocze - do decyzji wlasciciela. ---
@230 = ~Fighter~
@231 = ~gladiator~
@232 = ~Gladiator~
@233 = ~GLADIATOR: The arenas of the city-states are the heart of Athasian entertainment. Gladiators are slaves and free fighters trained to win crowds as much as fights.

Fighter subclass (Dark Sun 3.5e). Hit Die: d12. Base attack bonus: full. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Reflex. Skill points: 4 per level; Bluff and Intimidate are class skills. Instead of fighter bonus feats: a bonus feat at levels 1, 5, 9, 13 and 17 (exotic weapons).

Combat Stance (1st, more uses at 3rd, 6th, 12th and 18th level): +2 AC for 5 rounds.
Uncanny Dodge (4th) and Improved Uncanny Dodge (8th).
Armor Optimization (5th, 10th, 15th, 20th) and Parry (14th): +1 AC each.~
@234 = ~Gladiator: Gladiatorial Performance, Mercy, Arena Guile and Improved Feint - description only.~
@240 = ~Ranger~
@241 = ~waste ranger~
@242 = ~Waste Ranger~
@243 = ~WASTE RANGER: Rangers of Athas hunt across the stony barrens and silt flats, where water is the price of every mistake.

(Experimental ranger subclass: Dark Sun conversion test. Test ability at level 1: Called Shot.)~
@250 = ~Druid~
@251 = ~guardian druid~
@252 = ~Guardian Druid~
@253 = ~GUARDIAN DRUID: Each druid of Athas guards one stretch of land, an oasis, a ridge or a dry river, and draws strength from the spirit of that place.

(Experimental druid subclass: Dark Sun conversion test. Test ability at level 1: Elemental Shape - Fire Elemental.)~
@260 = ~Bard~
@261 = ~athasian bard~
@262 = ~Athasian Bard~
@263 = ~ATHASIAN BARD: In the city-states bards are entertainers, informants and poisoners for hire, welcome at every noble's table and trusted at none.

Bard subclass (Dark Sun 3.5e). Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Reflex, Will. Skill points: 6 per level. Mental Resistance (5th level): +2 to Will saves.

Spells: none - the Athasian bard casts no spells (poisons and bardic music instead).~
@264 = ~Athasian Bard: Smuggler, Poison Use, Streetsmart and Trade Secrets - description only.~
@270 = ~Sorcerer~
@271 = ~psion~
@272 = ~Psion~
@273 = ~PSION: On Athas the power of the mind is as common as magic is feared. Psions train the Way to bend matter and thought with will alone.

Sorcerer subclass (Dark Sun 3.5e / Expanded Psionics Handbook). Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 2 per level.

Powers: psion power list - psionic powers represented by the nearest spells of the game (e.g. Mind Thrust = Magic Missile, Inertial Armor = Mage Armor, Energy Bolt = Lightning Bolt), cast like sorcerer spells.~

// --- Podklasy test25 (komponent 2): lotrzyk, czarodziej, drugi kaplan. Nazwy i opisy robocze - do decyzji wlasciciela. ---
@280 = ~Rogue~
@281 = ~athasian rogue~
@282 = ~Athasian Rogue~
@283 = ~ATHASIAN ROGUE: In the city-states of Athas thieves, smugglers and spies thrive in the shadow of the templars, trading in water, metal and secrets.

(Experimental rogue subclass: Dark Sun conversion test. Test ability at level 1: Invisibility.)~
@291 = ~preserver~
@292 = ~Preserver~
@293 = ~PRESERVER: Arcane magic on Athas draws life from the land itself. Preservers take only what the land can spare and are hunted by templars and defilers alike.

(Experimental wizard subclass: Dark Sun conversion test. Test ability at level 1: Spell Shield.)~
@311 = ~barbarian warrior~
@312 = ~Barbarian Warrior~
@313 = ~BARBARIAN WARRIOR: The barbarian as a fighter subclass. Tribes of the wastes and the slave villages raise warriors who fight with fury rather than drill.

(Experimental fighter subclass, test29: barbarian moved from its own class. No fighter bonus feats (FEATCLAS column BARBARIAN_F), 4 skill points per level (SKILLPTS), Uncanny Dodge (DSKLASY), d12 hit die, rage and fast movement from CLABDS12.)~
@320 = ~Prestige Class~
@324 = ~PRESTIGE CLASS: specialised paths open only to experienced characters. On the next screen choose one of the prestige classes whose requirements your character meets (level, attack bonus, class level, race, feats, skills).

A prestige class has at most 10 levels and does not count towards the multiclass experience penalty.~
@325 = ~More prestige classes...~
@321 = ~arena champion~
@322 = ~Arena Champion~
@323 = ~ARENA CHAMPION (prestige class): Gladiators who survive enough bouts in the arenas of Tyr, Urik or Balic become champions, idols of the crowd and valuable property of their owners.

Requirements: character level 5, base attack bonus +5, Gladiator (Fighter subclass) level 5.

(Experimental prestige class, test30: d10, fighter attack bonus and saves. Test ability at level 1: Called Shot.)~
@331 = ~arch-defiler~
@332 = ~Arch-Defiler~
@333 = ~ARCH-DEFILER (prestige class): Defilers who drain ever more life from the land for their spells, on the path that once created the Sorcerer-Kings and the Dragon.

Requirements: character level 7, Wizard level 7.

(Experimental prestige class, test34: d4, wizard attack bonus and saves. Each Arch-Defiler level counts as a wizard level for spell slots (+1 spellcasting level of the wizard class). Test ability at level 1: Spell Shield.)~
@341 = ~dwarven defender~
@342 = ~Dwarven Defender~
@343 = ~DWARVEN DEFENDER (prestige class): Dwarves who make the defence of their focus - a village, a well, a mine - the whole purpose of their lives. A line of defenders holds better than a wall.

Requirements: dwarf, lawful alignment, base attack bonus +7, feats Dodge and Toughness.

(Experimental prestige class, test33: d12, fighter attack bonus, good Fortitude and Will. +1 AC at levels 1, 4, 7 and 10, Defensive Stance at 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9 (one use per day each), Uncanny Dodge at 2 and 6, damage reduction 3/- at 6 and 10.)~
@344 = ~Defensive Stance~
@351 = ~assassin~
@352 = ~Assassin~
@353 = ~ASSASSIN (prestige class): Killers for hire of the merchant houses and the templars of the city-states, masters of the quiet death.

Requirements: evil alignment, Hide 8 ranks, Move Silently 8 ranks.

(Experimental prestige class, test33: d6, medium attack bonus, good Reflex. Sneak attack like a rogue of the same level, Uncanny Dodge at 2 and 5, Invisibility at 4 and 8. Death attack and poison use - next tests.)~
@361 = ~elementalist~
@362 = ~Elementalist~
@363 = ~ELEMENTALIST (prestige class): Clerics who devote themselves entirely to their patron element and gain mastery over it unrivalled by any other being.

Requirements: cleric level 5 (able to cast 3rd-level divine spells). Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Each level adds +1 level of cleric spellcasting (Dark Sun 3.5e).~
@301 = ~fire cleric~
@302 = ~Fire Cleric~
@303 = ~FIRE CLERIC: Clerics of Fire serve the elemental plane of flame, the most destructive of the four elements under the crimson sun of Athas.

(Experimental cleric patron: Dark Sun conversion test. Test ability at level 1: Ilmater's Endurance.)~

// karta postaci (test28): cechy rasy pod nazwa rasy
@121 = ~Thrown weapons and slings, to hit~
@122 = ~To hit against~
@123 = ~aberrations~
@124 = ~AC against giants and ogres~

// test41: nowe klasy bazowe jako podklasy (Complete Warrior, Player's Handbook II, Complete Adventurer,
// Complete Arcane, Complete Divine) - opisy wlasne, zdolnosci przyblizone do mechaniki IWD2
@401 = ~samurai~
@402 = ~Samurai~
@403 = ~SAMURAI (fighter subclass): Sworn swordsmen bound by a strict code of honour, the samurai fight with a long and a short blade at once. On Athas they serve noble houses and city-states as duellists and bodyguards.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Fortitude. Skill points: 2 per level. Alignment: any lawful.

Class features:
- Two Swords as One (level 2): two bonus feats at once - take Ambidexterity and Two-Weapon Fighting.
- Kiai Smite (level 3, more uses at 8 and 14): a war cry that adds +3 to attack and damage rolls for one round.
- Bonus feats at levels 6, 10, 15 and 20.
- Staredown (level 6) and Mass Staredown (level 14): terrifying glare (Fear).
- Iaijutsu Master (level 11): +1 to attack and damage rolls.

Unlike the fighter, the samurai receives no bonus feat at levels 1, 4, 8, 12...~
@404 = ~Two Swords as One: bonus feats Ambidexterity and Two-Weapon Fighting (chosen at level 2).~
@405 = ~Kiai Smite: once per day per use, +3 to attack and damage rolls for one round.~
@406 = ~Staredown: a glare that frightens enemies (Fear).~
@407 = ~Iaijutsu Master: +1 to attack and damage rolls (in the rules a quick-draw strike; IWD2 has no initiative).~
@408 = ~Kiai Smite~

@411 = ~swashbuckler~
@412 = ~Swashbuckler~
@413 = ~SWASHBUCKLER (fighter subclass): Duellists who trust speed, wit and a light blade more than heavy armour. Arena favourites and caravan guards of the free cities.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Fortitude. Skill points: 4 per level. Alignment: any.

Class features:
- Weapon Finesse (level 1): one bonus feat - take Weapon Finesse.
- Grace (level 2): +1 Reflex save; +2 at level 11, +3 at level 20.
- Insightful Strike (level 3): +2 damage with every attack (in the rules: Intelligence bonus; here a fixed bonus).
- Dodge Bonus (level 5): +1 Armor Class; +1 more at levels 10, 15 and 20.
- Lucky (level 11): once per day +4 to all saving throws for one round.
- Slippery Mind (level 17): +2 to Will saves.
- Acrobatic Charge (7), Improved Flanking (8), Acrobatic Skill Mastery (13), Weakening Critical (14), Wounding Critical (19): described on the character sheet only.

The swashbuckler receives no other bonus feats.~
@414 = ~Grace: +1 to Reflex saving throws.~
@415 = ~Insightful Strike: +2 to damage rolls.~
@416 = ~Dodge Bonus: +1 to Armor Class.~
@417 = ~Acrobatic and quick-witted: acrobatic charge, improved flanking, acrobatic skill mastery, weakening and wounding criticals (description only). Lucky (level 11): once per day +4 to all saves for one round. Slippery Mind (level 17): +2 to Will saves.~

@421 = ~knight~
@422 = ~Knight~
@423 = ~KNIGHT (fighter subclass): Armoured champions who live by a code of chivalry, protect the weak and challenge the strongest enemy on the field. On Athas, rare paragons serving a noble house or a free village.

Hit Die: d12. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Will. Skill points: 2 per level. Alignment: any lawful.

Class features:
- Fighting Challenge (level 1, more uses at 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20): +1 to attack, damage and Will saves for one minute.
- Shield Block (level 2): +1 Armor Class; +1 more at levels 6 and 11 (in the rules only with a shield).
- Bulwark of Defense (3), Armor Mastery (4 and 9), Test of Mettle (5), Vigilant Defender (7): described on the character sheet only.
- Daunting Challenge (level 11): a challenge that frightens weaker foes (Fear).

Knights get no bonus feats; mounted abilities of the class do not exist in IWD2.~
@424 = ~Fighting Challenge: +1 to attack, damage and Will saving throws for one minute.~
@425 = ~Shield Block: +1 to Armor Class.~
@426 = ~Knight's code: bulwark of defense, armor mastery, test of mettle and vigilant defender (description only).~
@427 = ~Daunting Challenge: a challenge that frightens enemies (Fear).~
@428 = ~Fighting Challenge~

@431 = ~ninja~
@432 = ~Ninja~
@433 = ~NINJA (monk subclass): Spies and assassins who mix martial arts with ki tricks. On Athas they serve merchant houses and the shadowy Veiled Alliance.

Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throw: Reflex. Skill points: 6 per level. Alignment: any.

The ninja uses the monk's unarmored defence (Wisdom and level to Armor Class, lost in armour) and speed, but not the monk's unarmed strikes and other monk abilities.

Class features:
- Sudden Strike (level 1): sneak attack, +1d6 every two levels.
- Ghost Step (level 2, more uses at 6, 10 and 14): invisibility.
- Poison Use (level 3): poison weapon.
- Evasion (level 8).
- Ki Dodge (level 6, again at 12): blur.
- Ghost Walk (level 14): improved invisibility.
- Great Leap, Acrobatics, Ghost Strike: described on the character sheet only.

Class skills: as a rogue, plus Concentration; no Use Magic Device.~
@434 = ~Sudden Strike: sneak attack dice like a rogue.~
@435 = ~Ghost Step: the ninja becomes invisible.~
@436 = ~Ki power: great leap, acrobatics and ghost strike (description only). Ki Dodge (level 6, again at 12): blur. Ghost Walk (level 14): improved invisibility.~

@441 = ~scout~
@442 = ~Scout~
@443 = ~SCOUT (rogue subclass): Outriders and pathfinders who strike and move, never staying in one place. On Athas they guide caravans through the wastes.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throw: Reflex. Skill points: 8 per level. Alignment: any.

Class features:
- Skirmish (level 1; stronger at 5, 9, 13 and 17): +1 Armor Class and +1 damage per step (in the rules only after moving; here always, but not in heavy armor).
- Uncanny Dodge (level 2), Improved Uncanny Dodge (level 11), Evasion (level 5).
- Battle Fortitude (level 2): +1 Fortitude save; +2 at level 11.
- Fast Movement (level 3): faster movement; more at level 11.
- Bonus feats at levels 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20.
- Blindsense (level 10): see invisibility.
- Hide in Plain Sight (levels 14 and 18): invisibility.
- Trapfinding, Flawless Stride, Camouflage, Free Movement: described on the character sheet only.

The scout has no sneak attack. Class skills: Wilderness Lore instead of Bluff, Diplomacy, Intimidate, Open Lock, Pick Pocket and Use Magic Device.~
@444 = ~Skirmish: +1 to Armor Class and +1 to damage rolls (not in heavy armor).~
@445 = ~Battle Fortitude: +1 to Fortitude saving throws.~
@446 = ~Fast Movement: faster movement.~
@447 = ~Wilderness craft: trapfinding, flawless stride, camouflage, free movement (description only). Blindsense (level 10): see invisibility. Hide in Plain Sight (levels 14 and 18): invisibility.~

@451 = ~wu jen~
@452 = ~Wu Jen~
@453 = ~WU JEN (wizard subclass): Mystics who study the spirits of the elements and bind themselves with strange taboos. On Athas they are hermits of the wastes, close to the elemental powers.

Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: as wizard. Good saving throw: Will. Skill points: 2 per level. Alignment: any non-lawful.

Spells: the wu jen list from Complete Arcane, as far as IWD2 has those spells - wizard spells without most evocation, necromancy and conjuration (no Lightning Bolt, Burning Hands, Web or Mirror Image), plus Fire Seeds and Whirlwind.

Class features:
- Elemental Mastery and Spell Secrets (levels 6, 12, 18): described on the character sheet only.
- Watchful Spirit (level 9): +1 to Reflex saving throws.
- Taboo: in the rules a personal prohibition; no mechanic in IWD2.~
@454 = ~Spell secrets and elemental mastery (description only).~
@455 = ~Watchful Spirit: +1 to Reflex saving throws.~

@461 = ~spirit shaman~
@462 = ~Spirit Shaman~
@463 = ~SPIRIT SHAMAN (druid subclass): Mediators between the living and the spirits of the land. On Athas they speak for the restless spirits of dead lands.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throws: Fortitude and Will. Skill points: 4 per level. Alignment: any.

Casts druid spells (in the rules chosen each day - here prepared as a druid). No wild shape.

Class features:
- Spirit Guide (level 1): described on the character sheet only.
- Chastise Spirits (level 2, more uses at 6, 10, 14): turn undead.
- Blessing of the Spirits (level 4): protection from evil.
- Ghost Warrior (level 9): described on the character sheet only.
- Spirit Form (level 11): blur.~
@464 = ~Spirit Guide: the shaman's companion spirit warns and guides her (description only).~
@465 = ~Chastise Spirits: drives off undead (Turn Undead).~
@466 = ~Ghost Warrior: the shaman's blows strike incorporeal foes (description only).~

@471 = ~favored soul~
@472 = ~Favored Soul~
@473 = ~FAVORED SOUL (sorcerer subclass): Chosen of a divine power who cast its spells by instinct, not by prayer. On Athas - mortals touched by an elemental plane.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Reflex and Will. Skill points: 2 per level. Alignment: any.

Casts cleric spells spontaneously, as a sorcerer (spells known and spells per day of a sorcerer, Charisma).

Class features:
- Deity's Weapon Focus (level 3): +1 to attack rolls.
- Energy Resistance 10 (levels 5, 10, 15): fire, then electricity, then acid.
- Wings (level 12): described on the character sheet only.
- Damage Reduction 3/- (level 17).

TEST: cleric spells in a sorcerer's spellbook - check casting, caster level and spell failure in armour.~
@474 = ~Deity's Weapon Focus: +1 to attack rolls. Wings of the patron (description only).~

// test43: klasy prestizowe z podrecznikow (Complete Divine, Complete Warrior) - opisy wlasne, mechanika przyblizona
@481 = ~inquisitor~
@482 = ~Inquisitor~
@483 = ~INQUISITOR (prestige class, Church Inquisitor): Priests who root out corruption, heresy and lies within their own faith. On Athas they serve the templar bureaucracy of the city-states; in the Realms, the great churches.

Requirements: lawful good or lawful neutral, Cleric level 3, Spellcraft 4 ranks, Knowledge (Arcana) 4 ranks.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throw: Will. Every level counts as a cleric level for spells.

Class features:
- Detect Evil (level 1, again at 5).
- Immunity to Possession and Charms (level 1): immune to charm and domination.
- Pierce Illusion (levels 3, 7 and 10): see invisibility.
- Discern Lies and Learn the Truth: described on the character sheet only.~
@484 = ~Discern lies and learn the truth: the inquisitor knows when he is being lied to (description only).~

@491 = ~blighter~
@492 = ~Blighter~
@493 = ~BLIGHTER (prestige class): Druids who turned their backs on the land and drink its life instead. On Athas they are the druids' answer to defilers - priests of the wastes and the dead earth.

Requirements: any non-good alignment, base attack bonus +4, Druid level 5.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throws: Fortitude and Will. Every level counts as a druid level for spells.

Class features:
- Blightfire (level 1, more uses at 4, 7 and 10): sunscorch.
- Contagious Touch (levels 6 and 10): inflict serious wounds.
- Deforestation, Undead Wild Shape, Sustenance: described on the character sheet only.~
@494 = ~Deforestation: the land around the blighter withers (description only).~

@501 = ~stormlord~
@502 = ~Stormlord~
@503 = ~STORMLORD (prestige class): Priests of the storm - of Talos in the Realms, of the elemental plane of Air on Athas - who wield lightning and thunder as weapons.

Requirements: Cleric level 5.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as cleric. Good saving throws: Fortitude and Will. Every level counts as a cleric level for spells.

Class features:
- Resistance to Electricity 10 (level 1), 20 (level 5), 30 (level 9).
- Shock Weapon (level 2, more uses at 5 and 8): destructive blow.
- Storm Walk, Thundering Weapon, Storm of Elemental Fury: described on the character sheet only.~
@504 = ~Storm walker: the stormlord moves freely through storms; his weapons thunder (description only).~

@511 = ~ravager~
@512 = ~Ravager~
@513 = ~RAVAGER (prestige class): Warriors of the god of slaughter, who spread terror and pain. On Athas, raiders of the elven tribes and slave-hunters of the sorcerer-kings.

Requirements: evil alignment, base attack bonus +5, Intimidate 4 ranks.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Fortitude. Intimidate is a class skill.

Class features:
- Pain Touch (level 1, more uses at 4, 7 and 10).
- Aura of Fear (levels 3, 6 and 9): cloak of fear.
- Cruel Strike (level 5): +2 to damage rolls.
- Cruelty: described on the character sheet only.~
@514 = ~Cruelty: the ravager's victims lose heart (description only).~

@521 = ~hunter of the dead~
@522 = ~Hunter of the Dead~
@523 = ~HUNTER OF THE DEAD (prestige class): Warriors sworn to destroy the undead. On Athas, the restless dead of the ruined ages; in the Realms, the servants of Myrkul and Velsharoon.

Requirements: good alignment, base attack bonus +5.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Fortitude.

Class features:
- Smite Undead (levels 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9): smite evil.
- Turn Undead (levels 2 and 6).
- Spurn Death's Touch (level 4): immunity to level drain.
- Positive Energy Burst (levels 5 and 9): holy smite.
- True Death (level 10): described on the character sheet only.~
@524 = ~True Death: undead slain by the hunter never rise again (description only).~

@531 = ~dervish~
@532 = ~Dervish~
@533 = ~DERVISH (prestige class): Blade dancers of the desert tribes, whirling through battle with a curved blade. Athas is their home as much as the sands of Calimshan.

Requirements: base attack bonus +5, feats Dodge and Expertise.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throws: Reflex and Will.

Class features:
- AC Bonus: +1 to Armor Class at levels 1, 4, 7 and 10.
- Dervish Dance (level 1, more uses at 3, 5, 7 and 9): +2 to attack, damage and Armor Class for one minute.
- Fast Movement (level 3).
- Movement Mastery, Elaborate Parry, Tireless Dance, A Thousand Cuts: described on the character sheet only.~
@534 = ~Movement mastery, elaborate parry, tireless dance and a thousand cuts (description only).~

@541 = ~purple dragon knight~
@542 = ~Purple Dragon Knight~
@543 = ~PURPLE DRAGON KNIGHT (prestige class): Officers of the royal army of Cormyr in the Forgotten Realms, who lead by example and rally soldiers with their voice.

Requirements: base attack bonus +4, Diplomacy 2 ranks, Intimidate 2 ranks.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Fortitude. At most 5 levels.

Class features:
- Rallying Cry (levels 1, 3 and 5): war cry.
- Inspire Courage (levels 2 and 4): prayer.
- Fear (level 4).
- Oath of Wrath, Final Stand: described on the character sheet only.~
@544 = ~Oath of wrath and final stand (description only).~

@551 = ~warpriest~
@552 = ~Warpriest~
@553 = ~WARPRIEST (prestige class): Priests who lead armies, rally the faithful and break the enemy's will. In the Realms, war-priests of Tempus; on Athas, battle-priests of the elements.

Requirements: base attack bonus +5, Cleric level 1, feat Combat Casting, Diplomacy 8 ranks.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: as fighter. Good saving throw: Fortitude. Every level counts as a cleric level for spells.

Class features:
- Rally (levels 1 and 3): remove fear.
- Inflame (levels 2 and 6): prayer.
- Mass Cure (levels 4, 7 and 10): cure moderate wounds.
- Fear Aura (levels 5 and 9): cloak of fear.
- Heroes' Feast, Haste, Mass Heal, Implacable Foe: described on the character sheet only.~
@554 = ~Heroes' feast, haste, mass heal and implacable foe (description only).~

// test43: nazwy nowych zdolnosci GA_
@561 = ~Dervish Dance~
@562 = ~Lucky~
@563 = ~Combat Stance~

// test45: klasy potworow (ukryte podklasy wojownika, nadawane CRE potworow przez komponent 8)
@601 = ~undead (monster)~
@602 = ~Undead~
@603 = ~UNDEAD (monster class): hidden fighter subclass for creatures of this D&D 3.5 type. Not available to players.

Hit Die: d12. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 4 per level. No fighter bonus feats.

Type traits: immune to poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, charm, fear and confusion; darkvision.~
