@901 = ~dune trader~
@902 = ~Dune Trader~
@903 = ~DUNE TRADER (prestige class, Dark Sun 3.5e): Agents of the great merchant houses of Athas: negotiators, smugglers and spies who travel with the caravans between the city-states.

Requirements: Diplomacy 7 ranks, Bluff 5 ranks, Mercantile Background.

Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 8 per level.~
@904 = ~Dune Trader: Open Arms, Fast Talk, Contacts, Bargaining, Dazzle, Agent and Allies - description only.~
@911 = ~grove master~
@912 = ~Grove Master~
@913 = ~GROVE MASTER (prestige class, Dark Sun 3.5e): Druids who guard a stretch of land for its spirit and strike down those who would defile it.

Requirements: Druid level 5 (3rd-level divine spells), Wilderness Lore 5 ranks, Forester. +1 level of druid spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 4 per level.

Abilities: Smite Intruder (2nd, 7th level: Smite Evil of the game), Invisibility (3rd, 6th).~
@914 = ~Grove Master: Animal Companion, Guarded Lands, Sustenance, Teleport, Nondetection and Timeless Body - description only.~
@921 = ~master scout~
@922 = ~Master Scout~
@923 = ~MASTER SCOUT (prestige class, Dark Sun 3.5e): Guides and pathfinders of the wastes, who move fast and unseen and strike before the enemy knows they are there.

Requirements: Wilderness Lore 8 ranks.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Reflex. Skill points: 6 per level.

Abilities: Blaze Trail (faster movement), Swift Strike (sneak attack from 2nd level), bonus feat at 6th level.~
@924 = ~Master Scout: Hard March, Uncanny Stealth, Favored Terrain and Swift Tracker - description only.~
@931 = ~poisonmaster~
@932 = ~Poisonmaster~
@933 = ~POISONMASTER (prestige class, Dark Sun 3.5e): Masters of the venoms of Athas, whose bodies grow hardened to the very poisons they brew.

Requirements: Alchemy 8 ranks, Envenom Weapon.

Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Reflex, Will. Skill points: 4 per level.

Abilities: Mental Resistance (4th: +2 Will), damage reduction (5th and 10th), poison immunity (10th).~
@934 = ~Poisonmaster: Identify Poison, Dosage, Poison Secrets, Extend, Empower, Maximize and Quicken Poison, Mind Blank - description only.~
@941 = ~templar knight~
@942 = ~Templar Knight~
@943 = ~TEMPLAR KNIGHT (prestige class, Dark Sun 3.5e): Warriors of the templarate who lead the armies of the sorcerer-kings and enforce their will with sword and spell.

Requirements: Base attack bonus +5, Diplomacy 2 ranks.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: full. Good saving throws: Fortitude. Skill points: 2 per level.

Abilities: Smite Opponents (1st, 5th, 7th, 10th: Smite Evil of the game), bonus feats at 3rd, 6th and 9th level.~
@944 = ~Templar Knight: Secular Authority, spell-like abilities, Fearless Presence, templar knight spells and Spell Channeling - description only.~
@951 = ~arcane devotee~
@952 = ~Arcane Devotee~
@953 = ~ARCANE DEVOTEE (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Arcane spellcasters who serve a deity of magic as faithfully as any priest.

Requirements: 7 levels of arcane spellcasting classes (4th-level spells), Spellcraft 8 ranks. +1 level of wizard spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 2 per level.

Abilities: Sacred Defense (2nd, 4th: +1 to saves each).~
@954 = ~Arcane Devotee: Enlarge Spell, bonus feat, Divine Shroud - description only.~
@961 = ~archmage~
@962 = ~Archmage~
@963 = ~ARCHMAGE (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Wizards who reach the highest mastery of the Art and bend the Weave to their will.

Requirements: 13 levels of arcane spellcasting classes (7th-level spells), Spellcraft 15 and Knowledge (Arcana) 15 ranks. +1 level of wizard spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 2 per level.~
@964 = ~Archmage: High Arcana (Arcane Fire, Arcane Reach, Mastery of Counterspelling, Mastery of Elements, Mastery of Shaping, Spell Power, Spell-Like Ability) - description only.~
@971 = ~divine champion~
@972 = ~Divine Champion~
@973 = ~DIVINE CHAMPION (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Warriors who fight in the name of a deity of Faerûn and carry its favor into battle.

Requirements: Base attack bonus +7.

Hit Die: d10. Base attack bonus: full. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Reflex. Skill points: 2 per level.

Abilities: Fighter bonus feats (2nd, 4th), Smite Infidel (3rd: Smite Evil of the game), Divine Wrath (5th: +2 attack, damage and AC for 1 minute).~
@974 = ~Divine Champion: Lay on Hands - description only.~
@981 = ~divine disciple~
@982 = ~Divine Disciple~
@983 = ~DIVINE DISCIPLE (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Priests who become the mouthpiece of their deity on Toril.

Requirements: Cleric level 3 (2nd-level divine spells). +1 level of cleric spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Will. Skill points: 2 per level.

Abilities: Sacred Defense (2nd, 4th: +1 to saves each).~
@984 = ~Divine Disciple: New Domain, Imbue with Spell Ability, Transcendence - description only.~
@991 = ~divine seeker~
@992 = ~Divine Seeker~
@993 = ~DIVINE SEEKER (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Agents of the gods who infiltrate temples and strongholds to recover relics and secrets.

Requirements: Hide 8 and Move Silently 8 ranks.

Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Reflex. Skill points: 6 per level.

Abilities: Sacred Defense (2nd, 4th: +1 to saves each).~
@994 = ~Divine Seeker: Sanctuary, Locate Object, Locate Creature - description only.~
@1001 = ~guild thief~
@1002 = ~Guild Thief~
@1003 = ~GUILD THIEF (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Members of the thieves' guilds of Faerûn's cities: burglars, enforcers and fences.

Requirements: Hide 4 and Intimidate 3 ranks.

Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Reflex. Skill points: 6 per level.

Abilities: Sneak attack +1d6 (1st), +2d6 (3rd), +3d6 (5th); bonus feats (2nd, 4th).~
@1004 = ~Guild Thief: Doublespeak, Reputation, Uncanny Dodge - description only.~
@1011 = ~harper scout~
@1012 = ~Harper Scout~
@1013 = ~HARPER SCOUT (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Agents of the Harpers, a secret society that works against tyranny across Faerûn.

Requirements: Bluff 4 and Diplomacy 8 ranks, Iron Will; not evil. Harper spells counted as bard spellcasting.

Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Reflex, Will. Skill points: 6 per level.

Abilities: Tymora's Smile (3rd: +1 to saves).~
@1014 = ~Harper Scout: Harper Knowledge, favored enemies, Deneir's Eye, Lliira's Heart, Craft Harper Item - description only.~
@1021 = ~hathran~
@1022 = ~Hathran~
@1023 = ~HATHRAN (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): The witches of Rashemen, who wield both arcane and divine magic and guard their land from the Red Wizards.

Requirements: Human, 3 levels of arcane spellcasting classes, Knowledge (Arcana) 4 ranks. +1 level of wizard spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Will. Skill points: 2 per level.~
@1024 = ~Hathran: Cohort, Place Magic, Fear, Circle Leader, Greater Command - description only.~
@1031 = ~hierophant~
@1032 = ~Hierophant~
@1033 = ~HIEROPHANT (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): The highest servants of the gods, wielding divine power beyond that of ordinary priests.

Requirements: Cleric level 13 (7th-level divine spells).

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Will. Skill points: 2 per level.~
@1034 = ~Hierophant: Special abilities (Blast Infidel, Divine Reach, Faith Healing, Gift of the Divine, Mastery of Energy, Power of Nature, Spell Power, Spell-Like Ability) - description only.~
@1041 = ~red wizard~
@1042 = ~Red Wizard~
@1043 = ~RED WIZARD (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): The specialist wizards who rule Thay, feared across Faerûn for their power and ambition.

Requirements: Human, wizard level 5, Spellcraft 8 ranks; not good. +1 level of wizard spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 2 per level.~
@1044 = ~Red Wizard: Enhanced Specialization, Spell Power, Specialist Defense, bonus feat, Circle Leader - description only.~
@1051 = ~runecaster~
@1052 = ~Runecaster~
@1053 = ~RUNECASTER (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Divine spellcasters who bind their spells into runes.

Requirements: Cleric level 5 (3rd-level divine spells), Spellcraft 8 ranks. +1 level of cleric spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude, Will. Skill points: 2 per level.~
@1054 = ~Runecaster: Rune Craft, Rune Power, Improved Runecasting, Maximize Rune, Rune Chant - description only.~
@1061 = ~shadow adept~
@1062 = ~Shadow Adept~
@1063 = ~SHADOW ADEPT (prestige class, Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting): Spellcasters of Shar who draw their magic from the Shadow Weave.

Requirements: 3 levels of arcane spellcasting classes, Knowledge (Arcana) 8 ranks. +1 level of wizard spellcasting per level.

Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 2 per level.

Abilities: Shadow Defense (2nd, 5th, 8th: +1 to saves each), darkvision (7th).~
@1064 = ~Shadow Adept: Shadow feats, Spell Power, Shield of Shadows, Shadow Walk, Shadow Double - description only.~
@274 = ~Psion: power points, disciplines and augmenting powers - powers are cast like sorcerer spells.~
@1071 = ~wilder~
@1072 = ~Wilder~
@1073 = ~WILDER: Psionic talents who never trained in the Way; their power erupts from raw emotion.

Sorcerer subclass (Dark Sun 3.5e / Expanded Psionics Handbook). Hit Die: d6. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Skill points: 4 per level.

Powers: psion power list (nearest spells of the game), cast like sorcerer spells.~
@1074 = ~Wilder: Wild Surge, Psychic Enervation, Elude Touch, Volatile Mind - description only.~
@1081 = ~psychic warrior~
@1082 = ~Psychic Warrior~
@1083 = ~PSYCHIC WARRIOR: Warriors who turn the power of the mind on their own bodies, enhancing speed, strength and perception in battle.

Sorcerer subclass (Dark Sun 3.5e / Expanded Psionics Handbook). Hit Die: d8. Base attack bonus: 3/4. Good saving throws: Fortitude. Skill points: 2 per level. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every 3 levels.

Powers: psychic warrior power list (powers of levels 1-6 as the nearest spells of the game: Inertial Armor, Expansion, Thicken Skin, Hustle, Inertial Barrier...).~
@1084 = ~Psychic Warrior: power points and augmenting powers - powers are cast like sorcerer spells.~
@1091 = ~psiologist~
@1092 = ~Psiologist~
@1093 = ~PSIOLOGIST (prestige class, Dark Sun 3.5e): Scholars of the Way who study psionics in the academies of Athas.

Requirements: sorcerer level 10 (5th-level powers); lawful. Hit Die: d4. Base attack bonus: 1/2. Good saving throws: Will. Each level adds +1 level of sorcerer spellcasting (powers).~
@1094 = ~Psiologist: Psiologism, Psionic Acumen, Psionic Rationalization, Forethought - description only.~
@1101 = ~Stealthy~
@1102 = ~STEALTHY:

You are particularly good at avoiding notice.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Hide and Move Silently checks.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1103 = ~Nimble Fingers~
@1104 = ~NIMBLE FINGERS:

You are adept at manipulating small, delicate objects.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Disable Device and Open Lock checks.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1105 = ~Deft Hands~
@1106 = ~DEFT HANDS:

You have exceptional manual dexterity.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Pick Pocket checks.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1107 = ~Wastelander~
@1108 = ~WASTELANDER:

You are an experienced survivor of the Athasian wastes.

Benefit: You get a +1 bonus on Fortitude saves and a +2 bonus on Wilderness Lore checks.

(Dark Sun 3.5e)~
@1109 = ~Drake's Child~
@1110 = ~DRAKE'S CHILD:

Your body and mind are unusually resilient.

Prerequisites: Strength 13, Wisdom 13.

Benefit: You get a +1 bonus on Fortitude and Will saves.

(Dark Sun 3.5e)~
@1111 = ~Persuasive~
@1112 = ~PERSUASIVE:

You have a way with words and body language.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Bluff and Intimidate checks.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1113 = ~Negotiator~
@1114 = ~NEGOTIATOR:

You are good at gauging and swaying attitudes.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Diplomacy checks.

(Player's Handbook 3.5; the Sense Motive bonus does not exist in IWD2)~
@1115 = ~Magical Aptitude~
@1116 = ~MAGICAL APTITUDE:

You are adept at spellcasting and using magic items.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Spellcraft and Use Magic Device checks.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1117 = ~Trader~
@1118 = ~TRADER:

You know how to strike a bargain in the markets of the city-states.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Bluff checks.

(Dark Sun 3.5e; the Appraise bonus does not exist in IWD2)~
@1119 = ~Field Officer~
@1120 = ~FIELD OFFICER:

You know the tactics of war.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Diplomacy checks.

(Dark Sun 3.5e; the Knowledge (warcraft) bonus does not exist in IWD2)~
@1121 = ~Bouncer~
@1122 = ~BOUNCER:

Your sheer physical presence makes others back down.

Prerequisites: Strength 15.

Benefit: You get a +2 bonus on all Intimidate checks.

(Dark Sun 3.5e; using Strength instead of Charisma for Intimidate is not implemented)~
@1123 = ~Epic Prowess~
@1124 = ~EPIC PROWESS:

Your mastery of combat keeps growing.

Prerequisites: Character level 21.

Benefit: You get a +1 bonus on all attack rolls.

Special: You can take this feat up to 10 times. Its effects stack.

(Epic Level Handbook)~
@1125 = ~Armor Skin~
@1126 = ~ARMOR SKIN:

Your skin is tougher than normal.

Prerequisites: Character level 21.

Benefit: You get a +1 bonus to Armor Class (in IWD2 a general bonus, not natural armor).

Special: You can take this feat up to 10 times. Its effects stack.

(Epic Level Handbook)~
@1201 = ~Cause Fear~
@1202 = ~Cause Fear
(Necromancy)
Level: Brd 1, Clr 1, Sor/Wiz 1
Range: Close
Duration: 1d4 rounds
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 creature
Saving throw: Will negates

The target is overcome by fear and flees for a short time. In IWD2 the target panics for 2 rounds; the shaken effect on a successful save and the 5 HD limit are not implemented.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1203 = ~Lesser Confusion~
@1204 = ~Lesser Confusion
(Enchantment)
Level: Brd 1
Range: Close
Duration: 1 round
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 creature
Saving throw: Will negates

The target becomes confused for 1 round and acts randomly.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1205 = ~Enlarge Person~
@1206 = ~Enlarge Person
(Transmutation)
Level: Sor/Wiz 1
Range: Touch
Duration: 1 minute/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 humanoid
Saving throw: none

The target grows to Large size: +2 Strength, -2 Dexterity, -1 to attack rolls and -1 Armor Class. The change of size and reach are not shown in IWD2.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1207 = ~Reduce Person~
@1208 = ~Reduce Person
(Transmutation)
Level: Sor/Wiz 1
Range: Touch
Duration: 1 minute/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 humanoid
Saving throw: none

The target shrinks to Small size: +2 Dexterity, -2 Strength, +1 to attack rolls and +1 Armor Class.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1209 = ~Expeditious Retreat~
@1210 = ~Expeditious Retreat
(Transmutation)
Level: Brd 1, Sor/Wiz 1
Range: Personal
Duration: 1 minute/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: caster
Saving throw: none

The caster's base speed is doubled.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1211 = ~Magic Weapon~
@1212 = ~Magic Weapon
(Transmutation)
Level: Clr 1, Pal 1, Sor/Wiz 1
Range: Touch
Duration: 1 minute/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 creature
Saving throw: none

The target's weapon strikes truer: +1 to attack and damage rolls. (In D&D a +1 enhancement of one weapon; in IWD2 a bonus to the creature.)

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1213 = ~True Strike~
@1214 = ~True Strike
(Divination)
Level: Sor/Wiz 1
Range: Personal
Duration: 1 round
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: caster
Saving throw: none

The caster sees the immediate future of the fight and gets a +20 bonus to attack rolls for 1 round.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1215 = ~Tasha's Hideous Laughter~
@1216 = ~Tasha's Hideous Laughter
(Enchantment)
Level: Brd 1, Sor/Wiz 2
Range: Close
Duration: 1 round/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 creature
Saving throw: Will negates

The target falls down laughing uncontrollably and cannot act.

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1217 = ~Divine Favor~
@1218 = ~Divine Favor
(Evocation)
Level: Clr 1, Pal 1
Range: Personal
Duration: 1 minute
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: caster
Saving throw: none

The caster gains +1 to attack and damage rolls for every three caster levels (minimum +1, maximum +3).

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1219 = ~Shield of Faith~
@1220 = ~Shield of Faith
(Abjuration)
Level: Clr 1
Range: Touch
Duration: 1 minute/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 creature
Saving throw: none

A shimmering field grants a +2 deflection bonus to Armor Class, +1 more for every six caster levels (maximum +5).

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1221 = ~Longstrider~
@1222 = ~Longstrider
(Transmutation)
Level: Drd 1, Rgr 1
Range: Personal
Duration: 1 hour/level
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: caster
Saving throw: none

The caster's speed increases by 10 feet (one third).

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
@1223 = ~Produce Flame~
@1224 = ~Produce Flame
(Evocation)
Level: Drd 1
Range: Close
Duration: instant
Casting time: 1
Area of effect: 1 creature
Saving throw: none

A flame hurled at the target deals 1d6 + 1 per caster level (maximum +5) points of fire damage. (In D&D the flame stays in the hand for 1 minute/level.)

(Player's Handbook 3.5)~
